        v
  *** VOID CONSTRUCTION ***                                  fold-chat.js:2888
        |- genGate.void (generate)     -> kind "generate"
        |- plan || liveDrop            -> "live" | "unreached"
        |- voidReport(record, ...)     -> "unreached" | "unsupported" | "partial"
        v
  render: buildMsg -> gapV=normVoid(rec.void) -> renderFacingPage | renderGap
                                                             fold-chat.js:1421/1452/1491


2. THE VOID: FIVE SHAPES UNDER ONE WORD
=======================================
The word "void" names five different objects. They do NOT agree on shape, on vocabulary,
or even on what `read` means.

  (a) CHAT GAP          producer voidReport()          fold-chat-channels.js:47
      { kind: "unreached"|"unsupported"|"partial",
        counts:{sentences,grounded},
        read:[{title,domain,url}],   <- pages READ that did NOT establish the claim
        tried:[engine...],           <- only filled when kind==="unreached"
        question, closeBy:[...] }

  (b) APP GAPS          producer unreachedGap()/liveGap()   fold-chat-gaps.js:119 / :136
      { kind:"unreached"|"live", counts, read:[...], tried:[...], attempts:[...],
        readFailed, note, question, closeBy:[...] }
      -> SAME name "unreached" as (a), DIFFERENT shape.

  (c) GENERATE VOID     producer genVoid()              fold-chat-genvoid.js:297
      { kind:"generate", reason, outputType, topic, missing, had, setAside, unblock,
        note, counts, read:[pageEntries], closeBy:unblock, retry }
        read = pages the turn HAD (USABLE)   * * * OPPOSITE MEANING from (a) * * *

  (d) SLOT TREE         producer projectVoid()          fold-chat-void.js:206
      { id:"v0", kind:"ask",
        status: "open"|"satisfied"|"contested"|"refused"|"unmeasured",
        basis: "declared"|"read"|"unmeasured", children:[...], events:[...] }
      -> a STATUS VOCABULARY, not a gap. Shares only the name.

  (e) FOREIGN VOID      penelope/agent records          fold-chat.js:1616, fold-chat-explain.js:659
      { kind, reason, satisfy?, source? }

  DECLARED KINDS: VOID_KINDS = ["unreached","unsupported","partial","live","model","generate"]
                                                          fold-chat-channels.js:32
  PRODUCED KINDS (a): only "unreached" | "unsupported" | "partial".  "model" is declared,
  labeled (channels:86) and never produced by any live code path.


3. THE PRESIDENT CASE, TRACED
=============================
  "Who is the president?"            (measured: 14-24 s; 1 of 3 runs wrong)
     classify -> research
     senseTerm -> "president"
     search returns:  President (Wikipedia, actually a disambiguation) | President (band)
                      | List of actors who have played the president ...
     applyGate/titleGate pass all three  (why: C7 -- looksDisambiguation is NEVER consulted
                                          by the read chain or the gate; "President" has no
                                          "(disambiguation)" suffix to trip titleGate)
     all three are READ -> webPassages
     model writes one sentence from memory (the pages hold no such sentence)
     coverage = { total: 1, grounded: 0 }  ->  voidReport -> kind "unsupported"
        read:  the disambiguation/band/actors pages (C3)
        tried: []   (facts are gathered only for "unreached")
     render: gapAnswerLine("unsupported") returns "" -> the ungrounded sentence STILL shows as
             the answer, with a small label "nothing retrieved supports this" (C8)

  ROOT: the ask was under-specified AND disambiguation pages are read as ground. The void
  then reports "unsupported" -- correct in letter, but it is drawn beside the answer it condemns.


4. THE VOID DEFECTS (the "fucked up on defining the void")
==========================================================
  C1  five shapes named "void" (a-e above), one word.
  C2  6 kinds declared, 3 produced; "model" is dead vocabulary.
  C3  `read` means "read but did NOT establish" in (a) and "usable pages HAD" in (c).
  C4  the strand's real gap (minimalGap "no sentence states this") is DISCARDED at
      fold-chat.js:2253 (only its reason string survives as strandWhy); the drawn void
      becomes kind "unreached" although pages WERE read (note patched at :2895, kind not).
  C5  fold-chat.js:2240 injects a gaps.js field (`attempts`) into a genvoid.js shape -> hybrid.
  C6  a "generate" void is produced+stored, but buildMsg's render gate nulls ownRec for
      generate/code (fold-chat.js:1451) and run() never sets meta.void -> neither of the two
      renderers that can draw it is reachable from the producing path.
  C7  disambiguation pages are read as ground; looksDisambiguation exists but is never called
      by the read chain or the on-topic gate.
  C8  an "unsupported" void is drawn as failure text BESIDE the answer it condemns
      (gapAnswerLine returns "" for unsupported/partial).
  C9  slot gaps (answercard GAP_LABELS) live entirely outside record.void -> two philosophies.
  C10 dead code: voidsAfterSearch imported, never called.
  C11 the warrant summary writes `context:"open: ..."` but warrant records `open: []`
      regardless of the void (fold-chat.js:1827/2851) -> the void never reaches the summary.

  THE SURVIVING READING: the void is not mis-implemented in one place; it is FIVE
  implementations that were each locally reasonable and never reconciled. The fix is one
  shape, one kind vocabulary, one meaning of `read`, and a calibration (see VOID-AND-FELT.md).
